          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Mystery of the Hexagon</strong><br>\nAmong Pascal's lesser-known interests was the mathematical puzzle of the hexagon. He discovered that the hexagon inscribed within a conic section had intriguing properties, leading to what is now known as Pascal's Theorem in projective geometry, which has implications in various areas of modern mathematics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Illness and Death</strong><br>\nPascal's health was always fragile, and he suffered from illnesses throughout his life. Despite his poor health, he continued to work passionately on his scientific and mathematical pursuits. He died at the young age of 39 on August 19, 1662, after a malignant growth in his stomach spread to the brain.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Pascal's Legacy</strong><br>\nPascal's legacy extends beyond his mathematical and philosophical work. His thoughts and ideas were compiled posthumously in the \"Pensées,\" a collection that delves into human nature and the Christian life. His work and inventions remain influential, demonstrating the breadth of his genius and the enduring power of his ideas.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
